# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with an idle keepalive.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD is
# PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * Remote Desktop (TermService) is started via Start-Service, so it runs
#     under the Windows service host (services.exe), NOT PID 1;
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep 60 }` loop.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the hidden admin account (with the special-
# accounts UserList registry hide) ALREADY exists, so a fix must remove/disable
# the account and clear the hide key; no process runs as PID 1 that a restart
# could kill.
